WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
One night, one town.

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.530
A bike is stolen.

3
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.090
A window is smashed.

4
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.850
A phone is snatched.

5
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.310
Only one victim calls the police.

6
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.700
The others shrug and walk away.

7
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.970
That's typical.

8
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:17.910
In the national crime survey, only about
36 per cent of incidents were reported

9
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.050
to the police.

10
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.700
So if most crime never reaches the police,

11
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.540
how can anyone count it?

12
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.370
In this mission, you'll find
out what makes an act a crime,

13
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.420
and the five main types.

14
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.420
You'll see why police figures only include
crime that is reported, then recorded.

15
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.380
And you'll try asking people directly.

16
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.860
What could go wrong?

17
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.730
Your mission: work out how anyone can
count crime that is never reported.
